  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with PCA n2000 (config_001) achieves 48.5% accuracy, while image-only with ResNet50 (config_010) is very weak at 20.8%, making RNA the dominant signal. Uncertainty: We have no information on whether multiprofile aggregation improves upon the single-profile RNA baseline. This experiment (config_002) isolates the profile-setting variable by keeping the same PCA n2000 encoder and adding multiprofile with avgpool aggregation, directly testing whether multiple cell profiles per sample carry complementary information. It is the best next step because it is the cleanest single-variable extension of our best-performing configuration, uses the simplest aggregation (avgpool) as a principled baseline before trying more complex alternatives, and its outcome will determine whether to invest further in multiprofile+transformer, better RNA encoders, or multimodal fusion."
}

